o explain","paskaidrot","PAS-kai-drot"],["to practise","trenēties","treh-NEH-tee-es"],["to pass an exam","nokārtot eksāmenu","NOH-kar-tot ek-SAH-meh-noo"],["to fail an exam","neizturēt eksāmenu","NEH-iz-too-ret ek-SAH-meh-noo"],["to write down","pierakstīt","PEE-eh-rak-steet"],["to listen","klausīties","KLOW-see-tee-es"],["to read aloud","lasīt skaļi","LAH-seet SKAH-lee"],["to think","domāt","DOH-maht"],["to count","skaitīt","SKAI-teet"],["to spell","burtot","BOOR-tot"],["to translate","tulkot","TOOL-kot"],["to graduate","beigt skolu","baygt SKOH-loo"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Latvian has \"tu\" (you, informal) and \"jūs\" (you, formal or plural). Verb forms change for each person. There is no he / she difference in the plural except for gender in the past: \"viņi\" (they, men) and \"viņas\" (they, women)."],"rows":[["I","es","es"],["you (informal)","tu","too"],["he","viņš","veensh"],["she","viņa","VEE-nyah"],["we","mēs","mehs"],["you (formal / plural)","jūs","yoos"],["they (m)","viņi","VEE-nyee"],["they (f)","viņas","VEE-nyas"]],"ex":[["I am a student","es esmu students","es ES-moo STOO-dents"],["you are tall","tu esi garš","too EH-see garsh"],["she is my older sister","viņa ir mana vecākā māsa","VEE-nyah ir MAH-nah VEH-tsah-kah MAH-sah"],["we are friends","mēs esam draugi","mehs EH-sam DROW-gee"],["they are teachers","viņi ir skolotāji","VEE-nyee ir SKOH-loh-tah-yee"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Latvian has no \"the\" or \"a\". Nouns end in -s, -š, -is, -us (masculine) or -a, -e (feminine). Plural masculine: -i (grāmata, grāmatas). Memorise the plural of each noun."],"rows":[["the book","grāmata","GRAH-mah-tah"],["the books","grāmatas","GRAH-mah-tas"],["the child","bērns","behrns"],["the children","bērni","BEHR-nee"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","māja, mājas","MAH-yah, MAH-yas"],["one book, books","grāmata, grāmatas","GRAH-mah-tah, GRAH-mah-tas"],["one cat, cats","kaķis, kaķi","KAH-tyis, KAH-tyee"],["two books","divas grāmatas","DEE-vas GRAH-mah-tas"],["the children","bērni","BEHR-nee"]]},{"id":"to-be-b-t","title":"To be: būt","text":["The verb \"būt\" (to be) changes for each person, and is also used for \"there is\"."],"rows":[["I am","es esmu","es ES-moo"],["you are (informal)","tu esi","too EH-see"],["he / she is","viņš / viņa ir","veensh / VEE-nyah ir"],["we are","mēs esam","mehs EH-sam"],["you are (formal / plural)","jūs esat","yoos EH-sat"],["they are","viņi ir","VEE-nyee ir"]],"ex":[["I am a student","es esmu students","es ES-moo STOO-dents"],["you are tired","tu esi noguris","too EH-see NOH-goo-ris"],["he is a doctor","viņš ir ārsts","veensh ir arsts"],["we are happy","mēs esam laimīgi","mehs EH-sam LIE-mee-gee"],["they are at home","viņi ir mājās","VEE-nyee ir MAH-yas"]]},{"id":"having-man-ir","title":"Having: man ir","text":["Latvian says \"to me is\": man ir mašīna (I have a car). The thing owned comes after \"ir\". For \"I do not have\", use \"man nav\"."],"rows":[["I have a car","man ir mašīna","man ir MAH-shee-nah"],["you have a car","tev ir mašīna","tev ir MAH-shee-nah"],["he / she has a car","viņam / viņai ir mašīna","VEE-nyam / VEE-nyai ir MAH-shee-nah"],["I do not have","man nav","man nav"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","man ir vecāks brālis","man ir VEH-tsahks BRAH-lis"],["I have a car","man ir mašīna","man ir MAH-shee-nah"],["I do not have time","man nav laika","man nav LAI-kah"],["there is a problem","ir problēma","ir proh-BLEH-mah"],["there is no water","nav ūdens","nav OO-dens"]]},{"id":"present-tense","title":"Present tense","text":["Verbs change for person. Regular verbs (like \"lasīt\", to read) take -u, -i, -a for I, you, he / she: es lasu, tu lasi, viņš lasa."],"rows":[["I read","es lasu","es LAH-soo"],["you read","tu lasi","too LAH-see"],["he / she reads","viņš / viņa lasa","veensh / VEE-nyah LAH-sah"],["we read","mēs lasām","mehs LAH-sahm"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","es ēdu maizi","es EH-doo MIE-zee"],["you are reading a book","tu lasi grāmatu","too LAH-see GRAH-mah-too"],["she works in a bank","viņa strādā bankā","VEE-nyah STRAH-dah BAN-kah"],["we drink tea","mēs dzeram tēju","mehs DZEH-ram TEH-yoo"],["they are sleeping","viņi guļ","VEE-nyee goolyh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The usual order is subject, verb, object: \"es lasu grāmatu\" (I read a book). The object ends change (a \"case\" ending): grāmata becomes grāmatu."],"rows":[["I read a book","es lasu grāmatu","es LAH-soo GRAH-mah-too"],["he drinks tea","viņš dzer tēju","veensh dzer TEH-yoo"],["a big house","liela māja","lee-EH-lah MAH-yah"],["a new car","jauna mašīna","YOW-nah MAH-shee-nah"]],"ex":[["I read a book","es lasu grāmatu","es LAH-soo GRAH-mah-too"],["he drinks tea","viņš dzer tēju","veensh dzer TEH-yoo"],["we go to school","mēs ejam uz skolu","mehs EH-yam ooz SKOH-loo"],["they eat bread","viņi ēd maizi","VEE-nyee ehd MIE-zee"],["the teacher writes","skolotājs raksta","SKOH-loh-tahys RAK-stah"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"ne\" before the verb: es nezinu (I do not know). Verbs become \"ne\" + verb. With \"būt\", \"nav\" replaces \"ir\": man nav (I do not have). Nouns after \"nav\" take the genitive."],"rows":[["I do not go","es neeju","es NEH-ay-oo"],["you do not go","tu neej","too nay"],["he / she does not go","viņš / viņa neiet","veensh / VEE-nyah NAY-et"],["it is not good","tas nav labs","tas nav labs"]],"ex":[["I want","es gribu","es GREE-boo"],["I do not want","es negribu","es NEH-gree-boo"],["I speak English","es runāju angliski","es ROO-nah-yoo ANG-lis-kee"],["I do not speak English","es nerunāju angliski","es NEH-roo-nah-yoo ANG-lis-kee"],["I like it","tas man patīk","tas man pah-TEEK"],["I do not like it","tas man nepatīk","tas man NEH-pah-teek"],["she is here","viņa ir šeit","VEE-nyah ir shayt"],["she is not here","viņas šeit nav","VEE-nyas shayt nav"],["I have a car","man ir mašīna","man ir MAH-shee-nah"],["I do not have a car","man nav mašīnas","man nav MAH-shee-nas"],["I understand","es saprotu","es SAH-proh-too"],["I do not understand","es nesaprotu","es NEH-sah-proh-too"],["we are tired","mēs esam noguruši","mehs EH-sam NOH-goo-roo-shee"],["we are not tired","mēs neesam noguruši","mehs NEH-eh-sam NOH-goo-roo-shee"],["he works on Sundays","viņš strādā svētdienās","veensh STRAH-dah SVEHT-dee-eh-nahs"],["he does not work on Sundays","viņš nestrādā svētdienās","veensh NEH-strah-dah SVEHT-dee-eh-nahs"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add \"vai\" at the start to turn a sentence into a yes / no question: Vai tu esi students? (Are you a student?). Answer \"jā\" (yes) or \"nē\" (no)."],"rows":[["Do you go?","vai tu ej?","vai too ay"],["Is it good?","vai tas ir labi?","vai tas ir LAH-bee"],["Is it right?","vai tas ir pareizi?","vai tas ir pah-RAY-zee"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","vai šī ir tava grāmata?","vai shee ir TAH-vah GRAH-mah-tah"],["are they here?","vai viņi ir šeit?","vai VEE-nyee ir shayt"],["do you like tea?","vai tev patīk tēja?","vai tev pah-TEEK TEH-yah"],["is it cold?","vai ir auksts?","vai ir owksts"],["do you speak English?","vai tu runā angliski?","vai too ROO-nah ANG-lis-kee"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words come at the start of the sentence."],"rows":[["who","kas","kas"],["what","ko","koh"],["where","kur","koor"],["when","kad","kad"],["why","kāpēc","KAH-pehts"],["how","kā","kah"],["how much","cik","tsik"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","kā tevi sauc?","kah TEH-vee sowts"],["who is he?","kas viņš ir?","kas veensh ir"],["where do you live?","kur tu dzīvo?","koor too DZEE-voh"],["when is the lesson?","kad ir stunda?","kad ir STOON-dah"],["why are you late?","kāpēc tu kavē?","KAH-pehts too KAH-veh"],["how much is it?","cik tas maksā?","tsik tas mak-SAH"],["which book?","kura grāmata?","KOO-rah GRAH-mah-tah"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Latvian possessives change with the gender and number of the noun: mans (m), mana (f), mani (m pl), manas (f pl). Your: tavs, tava. His, her: viņa, viņas (no change). \"Patikt\" means \"to please\": man patīk tēja (tea pleases me)."],"rows":[["my book","mana grāmata","MAH-nah GRAH-mah-tah"],["my father","mans tēvs","mans tehvs"],["your book","tava grāmata","TAH-vah GRAH-mah-tah"],["his / her book","viņa grāmata","VEE-nyah GRAH-mah-tah"]],"ex":[["my phone","mans telefons","mans TEH-leh-fons"],["your house (formal)","jūsu māja","YOO-soo MAH-yah"],["his sister","viņa māsa","VEE-nyah MAH-sah"],["I like music","man patīk mūzika","man pah-TEEK MOO-zee-kah"],["I love football","es mīlu futbolu","es MEE-loo FOOT-boh-loo"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Use \"jūs\" (and \"jūs esat\") for one older person, a stranger or in a formal setting. Use \"tu\" with friends, family and children."],"rows":[["sir","kungs","koongs"],["madam","kundze","KOON-dzeh"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","kā tev iet?","kah tev ee-ET"],["how are you? (formal)","kā jums iet?","kah yooms ee-ET"],["where are you going? (informal)","kurp tu ej?","koorp too ay"],["where are you going? (formal)","kurp jūs ejat?","koorp yoos EH-yat"],["please sit down (formal)","lūdzu, apsēdieties","LOO-dzoo, AP-seh-dee-eh-tee-es"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: past forms of verbs (es lasīju, I read). Future: end in -šu (es lasīšu, I will read). A form changes by gender in the past of \"būt\": es biju, tu biji, viņš bija."],"rows":[["I ate","es ēdu","es EH-doo"],["I will eat","es ēdīšu","es EH-dee-shoo"],["I will go tomorrow","es iešu rīt","es EE-eh-shoo reet"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","vakar es biju noguris","VAH-kar es BEE-yoo NOH-goo-ris"],["I will study tomorrow","rīt es mācīšos","reet es MAH-tsee-shos"],["we went to the park","mēs gājām uz parku","mehs GAH-yahm ooz PAR-koo"],["I saw him","es viņu redzēju","es VEE-nyoo REH-dzeh-yoo"],["she wrote a letter","viņa uzrakstīja vēstuli","VEE-nyah OOZ-rak-stee-yah VEHS-too-lee"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Use the \"tu\" form: ej! (go!), nāc! (come!). Add \"-iet\" for \"jūs\": ejiet! For \"do not\", use \"neej!\" or \"nenāc!\"."],"rows":[["come!","nāc!","nahts"],["wait!","gaidi!","GAI-dee"],["do not go","neej","nay"],["please wait","lūdzu, pagaidiet","LOO-dzoo, PAH-gai-dee-et"]],"ex":[["come here","nāc šeit","nahts shayt"],["do not come here","nenāc šeit","NEH-nahts shayt"],["sit down","apsēdies","AP-seh-dee-es"],["do not sit down","neapsēdies","NEH-ap-seh-dee-es"],["be quiet","esi kluss","EH-see klooss"],["do not be late","nekavē","NEH-kah-veh"],["open the door","atver durvis","AT-ver DOOR-vis"],["close the window","aizver logu","AIZ-ver LOH-goo"],["listen to me","klausies mani","KLOW-see-es MAH-nee"],["do not worry","nesatraucies","NEH-sah-trow-tsee-es"],["speak slowly","runā lēnām","ROO-nah LEH-nahm"],["wait a moment","uzgaidi mirkli","OOZ-gai-dee MEERK-lee"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["\"Varēt\" (can), \"vajadzēt\" or \"drīkstēt\" (must / may) and \"gribēt\" (want) change for person. They are followed by the \"to\" form of the verb: es varu peldēt (I can swim)."],"rows":[["I can swim","es varu peldēt","es VAH-roo PEL-det"],["I must go","man jāiet","man YAH-ee-et"],["I want to go","es gribu iet","es GREE-boo ee-et"],["may I?","vai drīkstu?","vai DREEK-stoo"]],"ex":[["I can swim","es varu peldēt","es VAH-roo PEL-det"],["I cannot swim","es nevaru peldēt","es NEH-vah-roo PEL-det"],["can you help me?","vai tu vari man palīdzēt?","vai too VAH-ree man pah-LEED-zet"],["we must go","mums jāiet","moomz YAH-ee-et"],["we must not go","mums nav jāiet","moomz nav YAH-ee-et"],["I want to eat","es gribu ēst","es GREE-boo ehst"],["I do not want to eat","es negribu ēst","es NEH-gree-boo ehst"],["you can come","tu vari nākt","too VAH-ree nahkt"],["you cannot come","tu nevari nākt","too NEH-vah-ree nahkt"],["she wants to study","viņa grib mācīties","VEE-nyah greeb MAH-tsee-tee-es"],["I must work today","man šodien jāstrādā","man SHOH-dee-en YAH-strah-dah"],["you must not run","tev nedrīkst skriet","tev NEH-dreekst skree-et"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Prepositions: \"uz\" (on, to), \"zem\" (under), \"blakus\" (next to), \"pie\" (at, by), \"tuvu\" (near), \"iekšā\" or \"ar locative\" (in): mājās (at home), skolā (at school). Nouns after a preposition change case."],"rows":[["in the house","mājā","MAH-yah"],["on the table","uz galda","ooz GAL-dah"],["under the table","zem galda","zem GAL-dah"],["at school","skolā","SKOH-lah"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","grāmata ir uz galda","GRAH-mah-tah ir ooz GAL-dah"],["the cat is under the table","kaķis ir zem galda","KAH-tyis ir zem GAL-dah"],["I am at school","es esmu skolā","es ES-moo SKOH-lah"],["I am at home","es esmu mājās","es ES-moo MAH-yas"],["the shop is next to the bank","veikals ir blakus bankai","VAY-kals ir BLAH-koos BAN-kai"],["the park is near the station","parks ir tuvu stacijai","parks ir TOO-voo STAH-tsee-yai"],["we meet in the morning","mēs tiekamies no rīta","mehs TEE-eh-kah-mee-es noh REE-tah"],["the lesson is at nine","stunda ir deviņos","STOON-dah ir DEH-vee-nyos"],["the key is in the bag","atslēga ir somā","AT-slay-gah ir SOH-mah"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Add \"-āks\" to an adjective for \"more\": liels, lielāks (big, bigger). For \"the most\", use \"visvairāk\" or \"vislielākais\". \"Nekā\" means \"than\"."],"rows":[["big, bigger","liels, lielāks","lee-ELS, lee-EH-lahks"],["good, better","labs, labāks","labs, LAH-bahks"],["the biggest","vislielākais","vis-lee-EH-lah-kice"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","liels, lielāks, vislielākais","lee-ELS, lee-EH-lahks, vis-lee-EH-lah-kice"],["small, smaller, the smallest","mazs, mazāks, vismazākais","mazs, MAH-zahks, vis-MAH-zah-kice"],["this is better than that","šis ir labāks nekā tas","shis ir LAH-bahks NEH-kah tas"],["this is worse than that","šis ir sliktāks nekā tas","shis ir SLIK-tahks NEH-kah tas"],["she is taller than me","viņa ir garāka par mani","VEE-nyah ir GAH-rah-kah par MAH-nee"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Taškenta ir lielāka nekā Samarkanda","TASH-ken-tah ir lee-EH-lah-kah NEH-kah SAH-mar-kan-dah"],["it is the cheapest","tas ir lētākais","tas ir LEH-tah-kice"],["the same as","tāds pats kā","tahds pats kah"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[["I am hungry","es esmu izsalcis","es ES-moo IZ-sal-tsis"],["I am thirsty","man slāpst","man slahpst"],["I am cold","man ir auksti","man ir OWK-stee"],["it is raining","līst","leest"]],"ex":[["he is a teacher","viņš ir skolotājs","veensh ir SKOH-loh-tahys"],["you (plural) are students","jūs esat studenti","yoos EH-sat STOO-den-tee"],["I am happy","es esmu laimīgs","es ES-moo LIE-meegs"],["she is at school","viņa ir skolā","VEE-nyah ir SKOH-lah"],["you are my friend","tu esi mans draugs","too EH-see mans drowgs"],["it is cold","ir auksts","ir owksts"],["I study English","es mācos angļu valodu","es MAH-tsos AN-glyoo VAH-loh-doo"],["he teaches maths","viņš māca matemātiku","veensh MAH-tsah mah-teh-MAH-tee-koo"],["they work every day","viņi strādā katru dienu","VEE-nyee STRAH-dah KAT-roo DEE-eh-noo"],["is this your book?","vai šī ir tava grāmata?","vai shee ir TAH-vah GRAH-mah-tah"],["are they here?","vai viņi ir šeit?","vai VEE-nyee ir shayt"],["do you like tea?","vai tev patīk tēja?","vai tev pah-TEEK TEH-yah"],["what time is it?","cik pulkstenis?","tsik POOLK-steh-nis"],["whose book is this?","kam pieder šī grāmata?","kam PEE-eh-der shee GRAH-mah-tah"],["how old are you?","cik tev gadu?","tsik tev GAH-doo"],["how do you say it?","kā to saka?","kah toh SAH-kah"],["your book (formal)","jūsu grāmata","YOO-soo GRAH-mah-tah"],["their house","viņu māja","VEE-nyoo MAH-yah"],["my phone","mans telefons","mans TEH-leh-fons"],["excuse me, sir","atvainojiet, kungs","AT-vai-noh-yee-et, koongs"],["please sit down (formal)","lūdzu, apsēdieties","LOO-dzoo, AP-seh-dee-eh-tee-es"],["come here (informal)","nāc šeit","nahts shayt"],["yesterday I was tired","vakar es biju noguris","VAH-kar es BEE-yoo NOH-goo-ris"],["I will study tomorrow","rīt es mācīšos","reet es MAH-tsee-shos"],["we went to the park","mēs gājām uz parku","mehs GAH-yahm ooz PAR-koo"]]}],"name":"Latvian (Latviešu)","id":"lv","flag":"lv","note":""}